rk3588-camera-dkms (0.1.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Replace Ubuntu's rockchip-cif with rkcif v7.3 plus a fixed stream stop.
    It now stops the capture at a frame end before stopping the source,
    and frees the buffers and dummy buffer only after the DMA is idle.
    The interrupt handler no longer takes the subdev state mutex. With the
    stock driver, repeated start/stop hung a ROCK 5B+ within a few cycles.
  * rkcif: on RK3588 skip the CRU reset in runtime suspend, which hung a
    ROCK 5B+ silently a few dozen streams in, and soft-reset the MIPI host's
    capture logic when a stream stops instead, as Rockchip's driver does on
    RK3588. The soft reset also clears the frame address the DMA would keep
    from the previous stream. Other SoCs keep the CRU reset.

 -- Peyton Howe <peyton@localhost>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

rk3588-camera-dkms (0.1.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Only recommend linux-headers-generic. Depending on it made
    apt-get -f install pull in the archive's newest kernel alongside the
    ISO's; the image build now installs headers for each installed kernel.

